window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51 The Invitation She Couldn’t Accept","paragraphs":["Eira looked toward Alpha Killian’s office.","She knew exactly who had stalled her exit paperwork.","Before Miles could stop her, she walked in and closed the door.","\"Alpha Killian, I gave HR the thirty days’ notice required by my contract. I need my last day confirmed.\"","Alpha Killian looked up. \"What’s the rush? Planning to go back to Hale and play house?\"","\"No.\"","The answer came fast and sharp.","First Alpha Sebastian had tried to force her back into the role of a dutiful wife. Now Alpha Killian was trying to control when she could leave her job.","\"What I do next is none of your business,\" she said. \"My notice stands.\"","His brow furrowed at her distant tone.","\"You’re really set on leaving.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"And if I refuse to sign off?\"","\"You can hold up the paperwork, but you can’t reject my resignation. When the thirty days are up, I’m gone.\"","Her blue eyes held his.","\"If there’s nothing else, I’ll get back to work.\"","She turned toward the door.","\"Wait.\"","Alpha Killian pulled the RFP from his desk and dropped it in front of her.","\"The Sovereign Processor Initiative is active again. It started as Dr. Thorne’s project, and it’s in your field. Join Sterling Group’s proposal team.\"","Eira did not touch the folder.","\"I can’t.\"","She had seen confidential material from the original project. Advising one of the bidders now would create a serious conflict of interest.","He paused, then added, \"If you think the secretary position isn’t suitable, I’ll transfer you to the R&D center. Effective immediately.\"","A tech company’s R&D center held zero appeal for Eira.","\"No.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression tightened. \"You didn’t even think about it.\"","\"I didn’t need to.\"","\"You’d have your own team, a full research budget, and access to one of the best private labs on the West Coast.\"","\"Still no.\"","Alpha Killian leaned back, looking personally offended by how quickly she had dismissed the company he had built.","Then he tried one last angle.","\"Lila is joining our R&D division after she graduates.\"","Eira paused.","His expression eased. \"Interested now?\"","\"That’s great for Lila. Sterling Group will give her good experience. After a year or two, Professor Chase can help her move into a federal research lab.\"","Eira could also put in a good word for her, but Professor Chase’s recommendation would carry more weight in Lila’s field.","Silence filled the office.","She had just called Sterling Group a stepping stone.","Alpha Killian pointed toward the door.","\"Get out.\"","\"Of course, Alpha Sterling.\"","Eira left without hesitation and quietly closed the door behind her.","Alpha Killian stared at the closed door, his jaw tight.","--","When Alpha Sebastian received the invitation, he called an emergency meeting with Hale Group’s senior executives and lead engineers.","He had been following industry rumors for weeks and had already ordered his team to prepare a basic proposal. Now that preparation made him look brilliant.","By the end of the meeting, the project team was in place, the deadlines were clear, and Alpha Sebastian had put himself in charge.","His executives praised him for staying ahead of the curve.","Once the conference room emptied, Alpha Sebastian picked up his phone.","For some reason, he thought of Eira first.","Then he dismissed the idea. She would not understand how important this was. She would probably say That’s nice and ask what he wanted for dinner.","He called Serena instead.","\"Sebastian!\" Her excitement sounded instant and real. \"I knew Hale Group would make the list.\"","\"If we win this, it changes everything.\"","\"It’ll put Hale Group on the map. If you need anything from me, just ask.\"","\"I don’t want to put you in a bad position. You’re bound by your NDA.\"","\"Then I’ll stay out of the technical side.\" She paused. \"Have you told your family?\"","\"Not yet. You’re the first person I called.\"","The answer pleased her more than it should have.","\"Let me tell them. You have a proposal to finish.\"","Alpha Sebastian smiled. \"The deadline is tight.\"","\"I figured. Go make it count.\"","As soon as the call ended, Serena contacted the Hale family.","\"Hale Group has been invited to compete for a major contract,\" she told them. \"Sebastian is buried in work, so I offered to pass along the news.\"","Luna Margaret was thrilled. \"I knew he would get it. He’s worked harder than anyone for this.\"","\"I thought we could celebrate tonight,\" Serena said. \"Nothing too big. I’ll make a reservation.\"","\"That’s so thoughtful of you,\" Roger said.","Luna Margaret agreed at once. Serena was already acting like the perfect future Luna, handling family plans without Alpha Sebastian even having to ask.","Then Serena added casually, \"Should we invite Eira?\"","Luna Margaret’s mood cooled.","\"Why would we? She’s made it clear she wants nothing to do with this family.\"","Serena hid her smile.","\"I only thought it might be polite.\"","\"You’ve done enough. Let Eira sulk wherever she is.\"","The mate dissolution agreement had been signed and filed with the Pack Registry. Under Pack law, the marriage would officially end once the thirty-day waiting period expired.","As far as Luna Margaret was concerned, even that was too long.","She wanted Eira out of Alpha Sebastian’s life and Serena officially recognized as his Luna as soon as possible.","Serena booked a table at The Eden Garden, a new upscale restaurant, and shared the details in the Hale family group chat. Alpha Sebastian received a separate text telling him they were celebrating there that night.","--","Across town, Luna Seraphina had made plans at the same restaurant.","\"My beautiful, kind, incredibly generous mother,\" Lila began, \"shouldn’t you be taking Dad? If he finds out we went without him, he’ll complain about it for a month.\"","Luna Seraphina laughed. \"If I take your father somewhere this nice, I have to sit through a business dinner disguised as date night. I’d rather go with you and enjoy the food.\"","\"Smart choice.\"","\"Besides, the restaurant belongs to my friend Monica. It just opened, and I promised I’d stop by.\"","\"If we’re supporting a friend, can I bring one too?\"","Lila was already reaching for her phone.","Luna Seraphina glanced at the screen. \"Eira?\"","Lila looked up. \"How did you know?\"","\"You’ve mentioned her at least six times this week.\" Luna Seraphina smiled. \"And lately, she seems to be the only woman who can hold the attention of both Sterling siblings.\"","\"She’s easy to like.\" Lila pulled out her phone. \"Can we pick her up at Sterling Group?\"","\"Call her first,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She may already have plans.\"","Lila sent Eira a quick text asking if she wanted to join them for dinner. Less than a minute later, her phone buzzed.","Lila grinned at the reply. \"She said yes.\""]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52 The Unexpected Encounter","paragraphs":["Luna Seraphina watched her daughter’s face light up.","\"You really like her, don’t you?\"","\"Mom, you have no idea how incredible she is.\"","\"Because she found the problems in your thesis?\"","\"That’s part of it.\" Lila settled back in her seat. \"When Professor Chase saw my revisions, he couldn’t believe I’d fixed everything so quickly. He thought I’d need weeks, maybe even a whole new round of experiments.\"","\"But that isn’t why you admire her.\"","Lila shook her head.","\"Eira grew up in an Omega group home. She came to Palo Alto with no family money, no Pack connections, and no safety net. She built a life and a career on her own.\"","Her smile faded slightly.","\"And now she isn’t even working in her field because Alpha Killian hired her as his secretary.\"","\"Your brother didn’t force her to take the job.\"","\"No, but he’s certainly making it hard for her to leave.\"","Luna Seraphina raised an eyebrow. \"Is he?\"","\"I probably shouldn’t have said that.\"","\"Probably not.\"","Lila smiled, then looked out the window.","\"Everything I have came from you, Dad, and the Sterling Pack. I’ve worked hard, but I’ve never had to wonder whether I could afford school or where I would live. Eira never had that kind of support, and she still made something of herself.\"","\"That doesn’t make your own work less valuable,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"I know. I just respect her. She’s brilliant, and she doesn’t need anyone’s approval.\"","Pride warmed Luna Seraphina’s expression.","\"You sound like a very good friend.\"","\"I’m trying.\" Lila’s grin returned. \"Honestly, I wouldn’t mind having her in the family someday.\"","Luna Seraphina laughed. \"Then your brother may need some help.\"","\"He needs a personality transplant. Most of the time, he says nothing. When he does speak, he sounds like he’s firing someone.\"","\"Some women appreciate a challenge.\"","\"Eira has suffered enough.\"","They were still laughing when the car pulled up outside Sterling Group.","Eira was waiting near the entrance. Her eyes widened when she saw Luna Seraphina in the car. Lila had forgotten to mention that her mother was joining them.","Lila lowered the window.","\"Surprise.\"","\"I noticed.\"","Luna Seraphina smiled. \"I hope you don’t mind me joining you.\"","\"Of course not. It’s good to see you, Seraphina.\"","\"Get in. We’re already late.\"","Lila moved over, and Eira climbed into the back seat beside her.","A security officer recognized the Sterling family car. Before it had even left the curb, word reached the executive floor.","Miles stepped into Alpha Killian’s office.","\"Your mother and Lila were just downstairs.\"","Alpha Killian looked up in surprise. His mother rarely came by without calling first.","\"Are they coming up?\"","\"Not exactly.\" Miles paused. \"They picked up Eira and left.\"","Alpha Killian had already started to rise.","He slowly sat back down.","--","The Eden Garden","The restaurant sat at the top of Riverside Tower. Greenery spilled from hanging planters, and the glass walls opened onto a view of the city. Soft violin music played in the background.","Eira’s olive coat fit right in with the garden setting.","Monica, the owner, came over to greet them.","\"Seraphina. Lila.\" Her gaze moved to Eira. \"And you must be new.\"","\"This is Eira,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She’s a friend of Lila’s and works with Killian.\"","\"It’s nice to meet you, Monica.\"","\"You too.\" Monica smiled. \"I’ve heard good things.\"","She led them to a quiet table near one of the garden terraces.","\"I saved you the most private spot I could, but we’re still in our soft opening, so another party is seated nearby. The Hales booked a family dinner.\"","Eira’s shoulders tightened.","Lila noticed at once. \"Sebastian Hale?\"","Monica nodded. \"That’s the one. Five guests.\"","Lila counted them in her head.","\"His parents, his sister, and Alpha Sebastian make four.\"","\"The reservation was made by Serena Winthrop,\" Monica said. \"She listed herself as Luna Hale.\"","Eira picked up her water and took a slow drink.","Lila’s expression cooled.","\"That’s interesting.\"","Luna Seraphina glanced between them. \"Isn’t she the woman who came with Alpha Sebastian to the gala?\"","Before Lila could answer, the Hale family arrived and took the table behind them.","Isabella’s voice carried across the room almost at once.","\"Serena, how did you get a reservation here?\"","The Eden Garden was still in its soft-opening phase. It had no public booking system yet. Most tables went to investors, friends of the owner, and guests with the right connections.","Serena smiled. \"A friend from the research council got me on the list.\"","\"Of course she did,\" Isabella said. \"You know everyone.\"","She started to sit beside Serena, then changed her mind.","\"I’ll leave that seat for Sebastian.\"","\"Has he said how far away he is?\" Luna Margaret asked.","Serena checked her phone. \"He’s in the elevator.\"","Isabella grinned. \"He texted you and not the family chat?\"","\"Don’t start.\"","Serena’s blush only made Isabella smile wider.","A moment later, a host approached with Alpha Sebastian.","\"Your party is right this way, Alpha Hale.\"","Alpha Sebastian thanked him and loosened his tie as he crossed the dining room. He had expected a quiet dinner with Serena, not his entire family.","His steps slowed.","They were all there, smiling and ready to celebrate.","Everyone except his wife.","\"Sebastian.\" Serena raised a hand. \"Over here.\"","He started toward them, then caught sight of the woman seated at the next table.","Long golden waves fell down her back. A white dress showed beneath an olive cashmere coat, and a pearl gleamed at her ear when she turned her head.","Something about her felt familiar.","Monica glanced toward the Hale table.","\"Sebastian Hale keeps looking over here.\"","Eira’s back stiffened.","She had felt his eyes on her since he entered the restaurant, but she refused to turn around. Whatever he wanted, it could wait.","At the other table, Alpha Sebastian finally set down his coat.","\"That’s Luna Sterling,\" he told his family. \"I should go say hello.\"","Roger nodded. \"Of course.\"","Serena stood with him. \"I’ll come with you.\"","\"That’s not necessary.\"","\"I’d like to meet her.\"","Before he could object, Serena slipped her arm through his. Alpha Sebastian hesitated, then let her follow him.","They stopped beside Luna Seraphina’s table.","\"Luna Sterling, good evening. I don’t believe we’ve been formally introduced. I’m Sebastian Hale, Alpha of the...\"","His voice trailed off when he caught sight of the woman beside her.","\"Eira?\"","He pulled his arm free from Serena’s without thinking.","The sudden movement made Serena’s smile tighten.","Eira looked up at him.","\"What a coincidence.\"","Her tone was calm, almost bored.","No anger. No questions. Not even surprise.","The distance in her voice bothered Alpha Sebastian more than anger would have.","Serena recovered first.","\"Eira, I didn’t realize you had dinner plans here.\"","The words sounded friendly enough, but the question beneath them was clear.","How had Eira found her way into Luna Seraphina Sterling’s private dinner?"]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53 Alpha Hale, You’re Hurting Her","paragraphs":["Eira lifted her chin.","\"I’m having dinner with friends.\"","Lila nodded. \"I invited her.\"","Alpha Sebastian and Serena exchanged a startled look. They knew Eira was close to Lila. They had not realized she was also comfortable around Luna Seraphina.","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze stayed on Eira.","Serena touched his sleeve.","\"Sebastian.\"","Then she turned to Luna Seraphina with a polished smile.","\"Luna Sterling, I’m Serena Winthrop. Dr. Victor Winthrop is my grandfather.\"","Luna Seraphina raised an eyebrow.","\"Then I’m confused. Your reservation asked the staff to call you Luna Hale.\"","Serena’s smile froze.","\"There must have been a mistake.\"","Monica spoke calmly. \"My staff used the title provided with the reservation.\"","Color rose in Serena’s cheeks.","\"I’m not Sebastian’s wife,\" she said quickly. Then she looked at Eira. \"She is.\"","Luna Seraphina turned to Eira in surprise. \"You’re married to Alpha Hale?\"","\"For the moment,\" Eira said.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. He caught her arm, but Eira pulled back.","Luna Seraphina’s voice cooled. \"Let her go, Alpha Hale.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked down and released Eira at once.","Serena frowned. \"Why didn’t you tell anyone?\"","Eira rubbed her arm. \"Sebastian spent four years keeping our marriage quiet. Ask him.\"","The answer wiped the last trace of satisfaction from Serena’s face.","Luna Seraphina looked between Alpha Sebastian and Serena, understanding settling over her features.","\"Eira doesn’t owe anyone an explanation,\" she said. \"She’s here as our guest.\"","Lila smiled. \"Exactly.\"","Luna Seraphina turned back to Alpha Sebastian. \"I believe your family is waiting.\"","The dismissal was polite but clear.","Alpha Sebastian kept his eyes on Eira. \"Meet me downstairs after dinner. We need to talk.\"","\"Okay.\" Eira’s voice was flat. Compliant.","Alpha Sebastian finally walked away with her.","Eira looked at Luna Seraphina. \"I’m sorry about that.\"","\"You have nothing to apologize for,\" Luna Seraphina said.","Lila picked up her menu. \"Good. Now can we order? Watching Alpha Sebastian get shut down made me hungry.\"","Eira laughed despite herself.","Luna Seraphina smiled, though questions remained in her eyes.","---","Back at the Hale table, Alpha Sebastian could barely follow the conversation.","Every few minutes, his gaze drifted toward Eira. He caught glimpses of her golden hair and the curve of her profile whenever she turned to speak to Luna Seraphina.","She was smiling.","That bothered him more than it should have.","Serena noticed every glance.","\"What happened over there?\" Isabella asked. \"And who was that woman you grabbed?\"","Serena forced a smile.","\"That was Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"What?\" Isabella’s voice carried across the room.","A server appeared beside her. \"Ma’am, please keep your voice down.\"","Isabella flushed and waited until he left.","\"That was Eira?\" she whispered. \"What is she doing at dinner with Luna Sterling?\"","Luna Margaret glanced toward the other table.","\"She certainly moves fast.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression cooled. \"What is that supposed to mean?\"","\"She’s trying to trade up,\" Luna Margaret muttered.","Alpha Roger gave a dismissive shrug. \"One dinner with the Sterlings doesn’t make her one of them. Alpha Killian isn’t going to make a divorced Omega his Luna.\"","\"Divorced?\" Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped toward his parents. \"What are you talking about?\"","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret exchanged a glance and shook their heads.","\"Nothing. Forget about Eira.\" Luna Margaret’s tone brightened artificially. \"We’re here to celebrate you.\"","She smiled at Serena.","\"And we have Serena to thank for putting all this together.\"","\"It was nothing,\" Serena said, pleased to have the attention back.","As dinner arrived, Alpha Roger leaned toward her.","\"This contract could change everything for Hale Group. If you hear anything useful, I hope you’ll point Sebastian in the right direction.\"","\"Dad,\" Alpha Sebastian warned.","Serena rested a hand beside her glass. \"I can help with public information, but I can’t discuss anything covered by my NDA.\"","\"We’re not asking for documents,\" Luna Margaret said. \"Even a small hint about what the review panel wants could help.\"","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"If Serena crosses that line, she could lose her position and face an investigation.\"","Alpha Roger sat back. \"Fine. Forget I asked.\"","Serena gave Alpha Sebastian a grateful smile.","\"Thank you for looking out for me.\"","She had ordered his usual steak, medium rare, with no sauce. It should have been exactly what he wanted.","Instead, it reminded him of Eira.","She used to know every small preference without asking. His coffee. His meals. Which tie he wore to Pack meetings. What he needed before he realized he needed it.","He had treated that care as if it came with the house.","Alpha Sebastian glanced toward her again.","Eira was laughing at something Lila had said. She looked more at ease with the Sterlings than she ever had at a Hale family dinner.","His steak suddenly had no flavor.","Alpha Sebastian pushed back his chair.","Serena caught his wrist. \"Where are you going?\"","\"To take care of the check.\"","At the host stand, he handed over his card.","\"Put both tables on this.\"","The hostess checked the reservations.","\"I can close out your table, Alpha Hale, but Luna Sterling’s party doesn’t have a bill.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Why not?\"","\"They’re guests of Monica Vale, the owner. She’s dining with them.\"","Alpha Sebastian paused.","He was used to being treated with respect because of his title. The Sterlings moved through a different world, one built on old friendships and quiet influence.","What unsettled him was not that Eira had entered that world. It was how naturally she seemed to fit into it.","She used to be the woman who revolved around him. Now she had friends, plans, and an entire life he knew nothing about.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","For the first time, he wondered how much of Eira he had never bothered to know."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54 You Reek","paragraphs":["As Eira and the others headed toward the exit, the Hale family arrived at the elevators behind them.","Luna Margaret’s face soured when she saw Eira.","\"You saw us earlier and couldn’t even come over to say hello? How rude.\"","Eira had expected this. Luna Margaret could turn anything into a reason to criticize her.","\"I didn’t want to interrupt your family dinner.\"","\"Your family?\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice sharpened. He did not like how easily she separated herself from the Hales. \"We’ll talk about this when we get home.\"","Eira looked at him but said nothing.","Alpha Sebastian could hardly explain the situation in front of everyone. Serena had planned the dinner and invited his family without telling him. Calling her out now would only embarrass her.","\"And show my parents some respect,\" he added. \"There’s no need for that attitude.\"","Before Eira could respond, Luna Margaret turned to Luna Seraphina with a tired sigh.","\"Please excuse her, Luna Sterling. Eira has never had much respect for family. At home, she can barely take care of her husband, much less the rest of us.\"","She wanted Luna Seraphina to understand that a nice dress and a few powerful friends did not change who Eira was. Once the marriage ended, Eira would never find another Alpha like Sebastian.","Luna Seraphina’s smile cooled.","\"I’m not sure why your son’s wife is expected to take care of you.\"","Luna Margaret stiffened.","\"In the Sterling family, we don’t expect a daughter-in-law to serve us,\" Luna Seraphina continued. \"We have staff when we need help. We also don’t expect her to wait on her husband. He’s an adult.\"","Luna Margaret’s face turned red.","\"I only meant that family should take care of each other.\"","\"Then the care should go both ways.\"","Luna Margaret had no answer.","Monica glanced at Alpha Sebastian. \"Alpha Hale, you might want to think about why you stood by while your parents criticized your wife. If you keep taking her for granted, you may lose her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hand tightened at his side.","He looked at Eira.","Lose her?","For four years, she had stayed with him even though he had given her almost nothing in return. She had never seriously threatened to leave. As far as he knew, nothing had changed.","\"Eira, I’ll wait for you downstairs.\"","He gave Luna Seraphina a polite nod, then followed his family into the elevator.","Once the doors closed, he turned to Serena.","\"Why didn’t you tell me you invited my parents and Isabella?\"","Serena blinked. \"I thought you’d be happy.\"","\"We were all sitting there like a family while Eira was left out. How do you think that looked?\"","He was still angry about the way Eira had called them your family, as if she had already decided she no longer belonged with them.","Serena’s eyes filled with tears.","\"I didn’t think about it that way.\"","\"Serena was trying to do something thoughtful,\" Alpha Roger said. \"Eira didn’t even bother to celebrate your success.\"","\"She didn’t know about it,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply. \"If she had known, she would have planned something.\"","A tear slipped down Serena’s cheek.","\"It’s my fault. I should have included her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression softened slightly, but his frustration remained. \"You should have told me who was coming.\"","The elevator reached the lobby, and Serena stepped out with her head down.","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret motioned for Alpha Sebastian to follow her. Outside, Serena was already waving down a cab.","Alpha Sebastian watched her leave, but he did not move.","\"I’m waiting for Eira. I need to explain what happened tonight.\"","\"Explain what?\" Luna Margaret snapped. \"You don’t owe her an explanation.\"","When Serena opened the cab door, Luna Margaret gave Alpha Sebastian a push.","\"Go after her.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned to his mother.","\"No. And while we’re at it, stop criticizing Eira every chance you get. I’ve spent years focused on work while she handled everything at home. She took care of the house and made sure all of us had what we needed. She’s done enough.\"","Luna Margaret stared at him.","\"You hired a housekeeper. Don’t act like Eira did everything herself. And do you even know what she’s planning to do?\"","Alpha Roger shot her a warning look.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes narrowed. \"What is she planning?\"","Luna Margaret quickly changed course.","\"She’s planning to make a fool of you. Look at how close she is to the Sterlings. How do you know she isn’t interested in Alpha Killian?\"","\"She wouldn’t do that.\"","No one knew better than Alpha Sebastian how much Eira loved him.","\"How can you be so sure?\" Luna Margaret demanded","\"Eira wouldn’t hide something like that from me.\"","Luna Margaret let out a bitter laugh.","\"Then what about Serena? She comes from a respected family, and she has stood by you for months. Are you really going to let people treat her like a homewrecker?\"","\"Mom, don’t say that about Serena,\" Isabella cut in. \"Sebastian and Serena were together first. Eira was the one who came between them.\"","The elevator doors opened behind them.","Eira stepped into the lobby with Luna Seraphina and Lila. They had heard every word.","Alpha Sebastian turned sharply.","\"Eira.\"","Isabella did not back down.","\"What? I’m not wrong. If Serena hadn’t gone abroad, Eira never would have had a chance. Serena should have been Sebastian’s wife from the beginning.\"","Eira looked at Luna Seraphina and Lila.","\"I’m sorry you had to hear this. You should head home. I need to deal with something.\"","\"You don’t have to stay,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"I’ll be fine.\"","Luna Seraphina studied her for a moment, then nodded. \"Call Lila if you need anything.\"","\"I will.\"","Eira walked them to their car and waited until they drove away. Then she returned to the Hales.","She ignored Alpha Sebastian and looked directly at Isabella.","\"If you want Serena as your brother’s Luna that badly, convince your brother to divorce me. That would be more useful than yelling about it in a hotel lobby.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her.","Divorce?","No. Eira would never actually leave him.","\"You think I don’t want that?\" Isabella shot back. \"I think about it every day.\"","\"Enough,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply.","He turned to Eira, and his voice softened.","\"I’m not divorcing you. Stop talking like that.\"","Then he looked at his parents.","\"Take Isabella home. Eira and I are leaving.\"","He reached for Eira’s hand, but she stepped away.","Alpha Sebastian told himself she was only upset about being left out of dinner.","\"It’s cold,\" he said, forcing himself to stay calm. \"Get in the car. I’ll explain everything.\"","\"I’m going back to Mrs. Thorne’s. I’m not going with you.\"","His jaw tightened.","\"Eira.\"","\"I said no.\"","Alpha Sebastian caught her wrist and pulled her toward the car.","\"Let go of me.\"","When she resisted, he lifted her into his arms.","\"Put me down!\"","He ignored her and carried her to the passenger side. He set her in the seat, then leaned across her to fasten the seat belt.","Eira pressed herself against the seat, putting as much distance between them as possible.","\"You reek.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"What did you say?\"","To Eira, his betrayal had tainted everything about him. Even having him this close made her skin crawl.","His hand closed around her chin.","\"What the hell is that supposed to mean?\"","A flash of panic cut through his anger.","Did she know about Serena? Was that why she had started acting so differently?","\"You just ate,\" Eira said coldly. \"You haven’t even brushed your teeth.\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55 What Are Your Intentions Toward Eira?","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian remembered how particular Eira was about keeping things clean. She never left dishes in the sink or clothes on the floor.","But she had been gone for days, and the house was already a mess.","\"When are you coming home?\" he asked. \"The house needs you.\"","Eira gave him a flat look.","\"You can afford a housekeeper, Sebastian. It would cost less than a diamond necklace.\"","His expression changed.","\"What is that supposed to mean?\"","Eira caught the flash of guilt in his eyes.","\"Exactly what I said. Why? Does it mean something else to you?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"Then why do you look nervous?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked away.","\"I’m not asking you to come back because I think you’re the maid,\" he said. \"I want you home because that’s where you belong. You can’t keep staying at someone else’s house.\"","His words reminded Eira of something.","She pulled out her phone and sent Martin a quick message.","[I’ve already had dinner, so please don’t have the kitchen prepare anything for me tonight.]","Alpha Sebastian noticed the phone at once.","\"When did you get that?\"","\"Recently.\"","\"What happened to your old one?\"","\"It barely worked. I should’ve replaced it months ago.\"","His unease grew.","Eira had new friends. She had changed the way she dressed. She no longer came home. Now she had a new phone he knew nothing about.","\"Why didn’t you tell me?\" he asked.","\"Do I need your permission to replace my phone?\"","\"That’s not what I meant. I could’ve bought you one.\"","\"No need. I can buy my own.\"","\"With what money?\"","Eira almost laughed.","\"Alpha Hale, I still take home four thousand dollars a month. It may not compare to your income, but it’s real money.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. He had never paid enough attention to know how much she earned.","\"Do you have to talk to me like that?\"","\"I answered your question.\"","He took a slow breath.","\"I didn’t know my whole family would be at dinner tonight. If I had known, I wouldn’t have left you out.\"","Eira looked up from her phone.","\"Then who did you think you were meeting?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s silence gave her the answer.","\"You thought it would be just you and Serena.\"","\"Hale Group is competing for a major federal contract,\" he said stiffly. \"Serena shared some public information and gave me general advice. Dinner was just a thank-you.\"","He watched Eira closely, waiting for her reaction.","She simply nodded.","\"Then why did you let her leave alone? That’s a strange way to thank someone.\"","\"I stayed because I told you I’d wait.\"","Surprise crossed Eira’s face.","Alpha Sebastian had let Serena leave upset so he could wait for her. That did not sound like him.","Unless he was feeling guilty.","\"If you’re driving me back, we should leave,\" Eira said. \"You may still have time to make things right with Miss Winthrop. What if she changes her mind about helping you?\"","\"She won’t.\"","\"You should be careful. I’m supposed to quit my job and stay home, remember? You promised me ten thousand dollars a month, plus the cost of my classes. If we have a baby later, that will cost even more.\"","Some of the tension left Alpha Sebastian’s shoulders.","She was still talking about quitting. About preparing for a baby. About a future with him.","So she knew nothing about Serena.","Eira noticed his relief, and a cold smile touched her lips.","He was easier to read than he thought.","\"I don’t need Serena’s help after this stage,\" Alpha Sebastian said as he moved into the driver’s seat. \"Anything more could put her career at risk.\"","He fastened his seat belt, then glanced at Eira.","\"Sterling Group received an invitation for the Sovereign Processor Initiative too, didn’t it?\"","Eira’s hand stilled.","\"Why are you asking?\"","\"You work directly for Alpha Killian. You must have heard something.\"","\"I know Sterling Group was invited to submit a proposal. That’s all.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes sharpened.","\"Have you seen their bid?\"","\"No.\"","\"You’re leaving anyway. Could you look through the proposal before you go? I only need the main points.\"","Eira stared at him.","He was asking her to steal confidential information from Sterling Group.","\"I’m not on the proposal team, and I don’t have access to those files.\"","\"Alpha Killian keeps you close. You could probably get access if you tried.\"","\"No.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned at her quick refusal.","\"He made you his executive assistant right when you were planning to resign. He clearly trusts you.\"","The thought seemed to bother him more than it should have.","Then he leaned closer, his voice low.","\"I saw the way the Sterlings treated you tonight. Don’t let Alpha Killian fill your head with ideas.\"","Eira held his gaze.","\"What kind of ideas?\"","\"That you’d be better off without me.\"","The irony was almost laughable. A moment ago, he had asked her to betray her employer. Now he was warning her not to betray him.","Alpha Sebastian started the car.","\"Just remember who your husband is.\"","--","The Sterling Manor","When Luna Seraphina returned home, Alpha Julian was waiting by the door.","\"You went to Monica’s restaurant without me?\"","\"You would’ve spent the whole evening talking business.\"","Before he could argue, Luna Seraphina turned to Lila.","\"Tell your brother to come home. I need to speak with him.\"","\"Yes, Mom.\"","Lila escaped upstairs and immediately called Alpha Killian.","\"Mom wants you home tonight.\"","\"What does she want?\"","\"No idea. I’m just the messenger.\"","\"You had dinner with her. You must know something.\"","\"I know better than to get involved. Come home and find out for yourself.\"","She ended the call before he could ask anything else.","--","10:00 p.m.","Alpha Killian walked into the living room and found his parents waiting for him.","He sat across from them.","\"What’s this about?\"","Luna Seraphina did not waste time.","\"Do you have feelings for Eira?\"","\"No.\"","The answer came a second too late.","Alpha Julian gave him a knowing look. \"Try again.\"","Alpha Killian frowned. \"Nothing has happened between us.\"","\"That wasn’t the question,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"Did you know she’s married to Sebastian Hale?\"","Alpha Killian’s expression changed. \"She told you?\"","\"I found out at dinner. Alpha Sebastian grabbed her arm in front of us and called her his wife.\"","Alpha Julian’s face hardened.","\"You’re interested in a married woman?\"","\"I didn’t say that.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Alpha Killian leaned back. \"What if she’s getting divorced?\"","Silence filled the room.","Luna Seraphina closed her eyes for a moment.","\"Killian, I’m going to ask you one more time. What exactly do you want from Eira?\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56 Do You Have a Photo of Dr. Crawford?","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian did not answer right away.","Luna Seraphina studied him. \"That hesitation is exactly what worries me. You’re not sure what you feel yet.\"","\"I know enough.\"","\"Do you?\" Her voice was gentle but serious. \"You know what Eira has been through.\"","\"Yes. Her marriage to Sebastian is ending.\"","\"And you know how she grew up.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened. \"Growing up in an Omega group home doesn’t define her.\"","\"No, but it shaped her,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She grew up without a family she could depend on. Then she trusted Sebastian, and he failed her.\"","Alpha Killian fell silent.","\"If you aren’t sure about your feelings, don’t rush into her life just because you want to protect her,\" Luna Seraphina continued. \"She doesn’t need to be rescued. She needs honesty, respect, and someone she can trust.\"","Her gaze held his.","\"So take the time to understand what you really want. If this is only anger at the way Sebastian treated her, let it go. If it’s more than that, be certain before you act. Don’t become another man who makes promises he can’t keep.\"","Alpha Killian looked down, considering her words.","Alpha Julian nodded. \"Your mother’s right. Don’t confuse wanting to protect someone with being ready to build a life with them.\"","After a moment, Alpha Killian met their eyes again.","\"I understand.\"","--","Winthrop Estate","The moment Serena entered the Winthrop estate, a housekeeper hurried forward to take her coat.","\"Miss Winthrop is home. Let Alpha Victor know.\"","Serena was the elder Alpha’s favorite granddaughter. Everyone in the main house knew it.","She greeted the staff as she crossed the hall, smiling and calling several of them by name.","\"Your grandfather is in his study,\" the housekeeper told her. \"He said you could go straight in.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Serena opened the study door without knocking.","Alpha Victor sat behind a large oak desk, reviewing reports from the Winthrop Pack’s research foundation. Several patrol maps were spread beside them. Even in his later years, his Alpha presence filled the room.","He looked at Serena over his glasses.","\"Ten days. I was starting to think your parents had locked you in their basement.\"","Serena smiled. \"They’ve been busy.\"","\"They’ve been busy for months, but I haven’t seen many results.\" Alpha Victor closed the report in front of him. \"What about you? The Sovereign Processor Initiative has entered the bidding phase. Where is the work you were supposed to publish?\"","Serena walked over and poured him a fresh cup of coffee.","\"Dr. Crawford hasn’t given me access to the approved research. I can’t publish anything or earn authorship if the core team keeps shutting me out.\"","Alpha Victor’s expression darkened.","\"You still haven’t been allowed into the lab?\"","\"No. I’ve been back for more than three weeks, and Dr. Crawford hasn’t even agreed to meet with me.\"","Serena sat across from him.","\"Everyone calls me Dr. Winthrop because they respect you. But no one asks for my opinion. The project team smiles at me and then leaves me out of every important meeting.\"","\"You were never promised access to classified data.\"","\"I know. I’m asking to join one of the approved research branches. I need work I can legally publish.\"","Alpha Victor tapped his fingers against the desk.","\"Professor Davies controls access now. Dr. Crawford makes the technical decisions.\"","\"That’s why I came to you. She isn’t only ignoring me. She’s ignoring your recommendation.\"","Alpha Victor’s expression hardened.","\"I’ll speak to Professor Davies.\"","\"I want to come.\"","\"No. I already used enough influence to get you onto the project. If we show up together, it will look like the Winthrop Pack is pressuring a federal research team.\"","Serena hid her frustration. She chose her words carefully.","\"Felix Shaw mistook someone for her at the gala. Has he ever met Dr. Crawford?\"","Alpha Victor gave a dry laugh.","\"His grandfather, Dr. Adrian Shaw, knew about her work. He and Dr. Thorne once competed to recruit her.\"","\"What about Felix? Has he ever met her?\"","Alpha Victor thought for a moment.","\" Dr. Crawford joined Thorne’s team seven years ago, while the work was still classified. After Thorne died, the program was suspended. It only restarted after she agreed to lead it.\"","\"So Felix wouldn’t recognize her?\"","\"He doesn’t have the clearance to access her identity records. If they met somewhere outside the project, I wouldn’t know.\"","It was not a complete denial, but Serena still felt some relief.","Alpha Victor studied her.","\"Why are you suddenly so interested in Felix Shaw? Did you see him at the gala?\"","\"Grandpa, you know I’m not interested in him. I already have someone.\"","\"Sebastian Hale.\"","Serena’s expression brightened. \"Yes.\"","Alpha Victor leaned back.","\"Hale Pack has grown quickly under him. Their territory has expanded, and their number of registered pack members has nearly tripled. He has also strengthened their patrol units and brought several smaller packs under Hale protection.\"","\"He’s a strong Alpha,\" Serena said. \"And while I was abroad, he invested heavily in my research.\"","\"Then focus on your own position before you worry about becoming his Luna.\"","The reminder stung, but Serena kept smiling. \"Can you tell me anything about Dr. Crawford? What she looks like? Where she’s from? If I could speak to her myself, I might be able to clear up this misunderstanding.\"","Alpha Victor shook his head.","\"Her identity is protected under federal security rules. Her photographs, address, Pack registration, and family history are sealed.\"","\"You don’t know what she looks like?\"","\"I’ve spoken to her through secure channels, but we’ve never met face-to-face. She avoids public appearances, and Professor Davies protects her privacy.\"","Serena’s heart sank.","\"So even you can’t help me reach her?\"","\"I can request a meeting. That’s all.\"","\"Dr. Thorne is gone. Professor Davies can protect her privacy, but he cannot shield her from every research council, contractor, and funding board.\"","His eyes turned cold.","\"No scientist works alone forever. Sooner or later, Dr. Crawford will need powerful allies.\"","\"We’ll remind her that the Winthrop Pack is better as a friend than an enemy.\"","That night, Eira received a text from Professor Davies.","Professor Davies: Victor Winthrop requested a meeting tomorrow at two. I need you there.","At the Winthrop estate, one of Alpha Victor’s staff quietly passed the same information to Serena."]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57 The Photograph Sterling Group Headquarters","paragraphs":["The next morning, Eira arrived at work as usual.","Most of the executive floor was busy with Sterling Group’s proposal for the Sovereign Processor Initiative. Eira was not part of the bid team, so she spent the morning arranging Alpha Killian’s business trip.","It was her first time planning an executive trip. She reviewed his previous schedules, confirmed the flights and meetings, then built a tight itinerary around them.","Every hour had a purpose.","When she finished, she emailed the schedule to Alpha Killian and submitted a request to leave that afternoon.","Half an hour passed without a response.","Eira walked to his office and knocked.","Alpha Killian looked up from his computer. For a moment, he simply stared at her.","\"Come in.\"","\"Alpha Killian, I submitted a request for this afternoon. I need to leave by one.\"","\"Where are you going?\"","The question left his mouth before he could stop it.","Eira waited.","Alpha Killian remembered his mother’s warning and looked back at his screen.","\"Never mind. Log it as personal leave.\"","\"Thank you.\"","She turned to go.","Alpha Killian watched her leave, annoyed by how much effort it took not to ask again.","--","Shortly before lunch, Alpha Killian passed the break room and heard Eira speaking quietly on the phone.","\"Do you think Victor Winthrop is trying to pressure me because Dr. Thorne isn’t here anymore?\"","Alpha Killian slowed.","Eira listened for a moment.","\"I understand. I’ll be at the institute by two.\"","She ended the call and turned around. Alpha Killian stood a few feet away with a cup of coffee in his hand.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","She slipped her phone into her bag and headed for the door.","\"Wait.\"","Eira stopped.","\"If this meeting has anything to do with your work here, tell me,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Sterling’s legal team can handle any outside pressure.\"","Her eyes widened slightly.","\"You heard me?\"","\"Enough.\"","\"This is a personal matter.\"","Alpha Killian studied her face.","\"Then I won’t interfere. But if anyone tries to use Sterling Group against you, let me know.\"","Eira had expected questions. She had not expected him to respect the line she had drawn.","\"Thank you.\"","Alpha Killian nodded toward her bag. \"Your schedule for my trip is finished?\"","\"Yes. The itinerary and flight details are in your inbox.\"","\"Good.\"","He returned to his office and opened her email.","The schedule was clear, accurate, and painfully efficient. She had booked an overnight flight, followed by a breakfast meeting less than an hour after he landed.","There was no time to rest.","Alpha Killian stared at the screen.","She had arranged the trip as if sleep were optional.","Then again, he had delayed her resignation paperwork and made her handle a job she had never wanted.","Perhaps he had earned this schedule.","--","Silix Institute, 1:30 p.m.","Eira arrived at the institute half an hour before the meeting. The autumn wind cut through her coat as she crossed the entrance plaza.","She completed the retinal scan, stepped inside, and took a mask from her bag. After putting it on, she tied her hair into a low ponytail.","Professor Davies was waiting in the lobby.","\"This meeting is about Serena,\" he said as they walked toward his office. \"I’d bet money on it.\"","Ever since the gala, he had stopped calling her Dr. Winthrop outside formal meetings.","\"She already has a role in the project,\" Eira said. \"What else does she want?\"","\"Publication credit.\"","Eira frowned.","The Sovereign Processor Initiative was classified, but several related papers had been approved for public release. Serena had already been listed as a senior consultant despite her limited contribution.","\"She’s already ahead of half the team on the author list,\" Eira said. \"What does she want now? First authorship?\"","Professor Davies did not answer at once.","He could not rule it out.","\"She won’t get it,\" he said. \"Your name has already been submitted as first author. I made sure of that.\"","\"Good. If Victor tries to give Serena credit for my work, I’ll file a formal complaint and step down as technical lead.\"","Professor Davies glanced at her. \"You’d really leave?\"","\"I won’t let someone else claim research they didn’t do.\"","He could not argue with that.","When they entered his office, Professor Davies closed the door behind them.","\"There’s something else I’ve been meaning to ask,\" he said. \"Is your divorce final?\"","\"Not yet. The dissolution agreement has been signed. We’re waiting for the Pack Registry to issue the certificate.\"","\"At least Sebastian signed it.\"","Eira noticed the edge in his voice.","\"It’s fine.\"","\"No, it isn’t.\" Professor Davies frowned. \"You spent years cooking for him, managing the house, and taking care of his parents and sister. Meanwhile, he was flying overseas to see Serena.\"","Eira went still.","She knew Sebastian had sent Serena money every year. She had not known about the trips.","\"He went to see her?\"","Professor Davies’s expression changed. \"You didn’t know?\"","\"No.\"","He hesitated before answering.","\"More than once. I thought you knew.\"","Eira looked toward the window.","Of course Sebastian had never told her. While she stayed home and kept his life in order, he had been crossing the ocean to see another woman.","The money, the trips, and the years of silence had all been part of the same lie.","Professor Davies watched her carefully. \"Eira?\"","\"I’m fine.\"","Her voice was calm, but her eyes had turned cold.","A black sedan pulled through the institute’s main gate below. A few minutes later, Serena stepped out and headed toward the entrance.","Eira watched her cross the plaza.","\"It looks like Victor didn’t come alone.\"","Professor Davies joined her by the window and frowned.","\"I told him this meeting was limited to authorized participants.\"","\"Serena has temporary access to the administrative wing.\"","Eira turned away from the window.","\"Let her wait.\"","--","Victor arrived at the institute shortly before two and was taken to a conference room in the administrative wing.","A few minutes later, Serena entered using her temporary project badge. Her clearance allowed her into the administrative area, but not the secure labs.","At the security desk, she smiled at the guard.","\"Has Dr. Crawford arrived?\"","\"Good afternoon, Dr. Winthrop.\"","He checked her badge but did not answer the question.","Dr. Crawford’s schedule was protected.","Serena kept smiling. \"Of course. Security rules.\"","She walked away before he could ask why she wanted to know.","The administrative hall had a small seating area near the conference rooms. Serena chose a chair with a clear view of the corridor and pretended to read something on her phone.","Ten minutes later, three people appeared at the far end of the hall. Victor’s assistant led the way. Professor Davies followed, with a woman walking beside him.","Serena narrowed her eyes.","Professor Davies blocked most of the woman from view. All Serena could see were plain slacks, flat shoes, and a dark coat. Nothing stood out.","As they came closer, Serena quietly turned off her camera flash and sound.","Professor Davies reached for the conference room door.","Serena raised her phone.","Three quick photos.","The group disappeared inside without looking in her direction.","Serena immediately opened her photo gallery."]}]);
